்","lemma":"போகுதல்","gloss":"if they go"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even if they go"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"விதுப்புற","parts":[{"text":"விதுப்பு","lemma":"விதுப்பு","gloss":"trembling"},{"text":"உற","lemma":"உறுதல்","gloss":"to experience"}],"gloss":"to experience trembling"},{"surface":"அறியா","parts":[{"text":"அறி","lemma":"அறிதல்","gloss":"know"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ஆ","gloss":"not"}],"gloss":"not knowing"},{"surface":"ஏமக்","parts":[{"text":"ஏமக்","lemma":"ஏமக்","gloss":"protective"}],"gloss":"protective","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"காப்பினை","parts":[{"text":"காப்பு","lemma":"காப்பு","gloss":"guard"},{"text":"இனை","lemma":"இனை","gloss":"you have"}],"gloss":"you have protection"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அனையை","parts":[{"text":"அனை","lemma":"அனை","gloss":"such a person"},{"text":"ஐ","lemma":"ஐ","gloss":"you are"}],"gloss":"you are such a person"},{"surface":"ஆகல்","parts":[{"text":"ஆகல்","lemma":"ஆதல்","gloss":"being"}],"gloss":"being"},{"surface":"மாறே","parts":[{"text":"மாறு","lemma":"மாறு","gloss":"because"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"because indeed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மன்னுயிர்","parts":[{"text":"மன்னு","lemma":"மன்னுதல்","gloss":"abiding"},{"text":"உயிர்","lemma":"உயிர்","gloss":"lives"}],"gloss":"abiding lives"},{"surface":"எல்லாம்","parts":[{"text":"எல்லாம்","lemma":"எல்லாம்","gloss":"all"}],"gloss":"all"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you"},{"surface":"அஞ்சும்மே","parts":[{"text":"அஞ்சு","lemma":"அஞ்சுதல்","gloss":"revere"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"will"},{"text":"மே","lemma":"மே","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"will revere"}]}],"literal":"The depth of the great ocean / and the width of the vast earth / and the directions where the wind blows / and the empty, enduring sky—thus / even if one could measure and know those, you are difficult to measure! / Your wisdom, mercy, and great compassion, / other than the fire that cooks rice / and the burning heat of the red sun, / those who live under your shade know no other burning heat. / Other than the rainbow, they know no bow of murder. / Other than the plow, they know no weapons. / While enemies perish along with skilled warriors, / O great lord who consumes the land of others! In your country, / except when pregnant women crave and eat it, / enemies do not eat your precious soil. / With a guarded fortress where arrows rest, / and an upright sceptre where righteousness abides, / whether new birds arrive or old birds depart, / you provide a secure protection that knows no trembling. / Because you are of such a nature, / all living beings in the world revere you.","translation":"Even if one could measure the depth of the vast ocean, the width of the wide earth, the directions where the wind blows, and the empty, enduring sky, you are difficult to measure! Your wisdom, mercy, and great compassion are boundless. Those who live under your protective shade know no burning heat other than the fire that cooks their food and the warmth of the red sun. They know no bow of murder other than the beautiful rainbow. They know no weapons other than the plow. O great lord who conquers the lands of others with your skilled warriors! In your country, unless pregnant women crave and eat the soil, enemies never taste your precious land. With a guarded fortress where arrows rest and an upright sceptre where righteousness abides, you provide secure protection that never trembles, whether new birds of omen arrive or old ones depart. Because you are such a ruler, all living beings in this world look up to you with reverence.","modern":"பெரிய கடலின் ஆழத்தையும், பரந்த பூமியின் அகலத்தையும், காற்று வீசும் திசைகளையும், வெற்று வானத்தின் எல்லையையும் அளந்து அறிய முடிந்தாலும், உன்னுடைய அறிவு, அருள், பெருங்கருணை ஆகியவற்றை அளவிடுவது கடினம். உன்னுடைய நிழலில் வாழும் மக்கள், சோறு சமைக்கும் நெருப்பையும் செஞ்ஞாயிற்றின் வெப்பத்தையும் தவிர வேறு எந்தத் துன்பத்தையும் அறிய மாட்டார்கள். அவர்கள் வானவில்லைத் தவிரக் கொலை செய்யும் வில்லை அறியார்; கலப்பையைத் தவிரப் படைக்கலன்களை அறியார். திறமைமிக்க வீரர்களோடு பகைவரை அழித்துப் பிறர் நாட்டை வெல்லும் தலைவனே! உனது நாட்டில், கர்ப்பிணிப் பெண்கள் மண்ணைத் தின்னும் ஆசையால் உண்பதைத் தவிர, பகைவர்கள் உனது அருமையான மண்ணைக் கைப்பற்றி உண்ண முடியாது. அம்புகள் ஓய்ந்திருக்கும் காவல் மிகுந்த கோட்டையையும், அறம் நிலைபெற்ற செங்கோலையும் உடையவன் நீ. புதிய பறவைகள் வந்தாலும், பழைய பறவைகள் போனாலும் கலங்காத பாதுகாப்பைத் தருபவன் நீ. இத்தகைய தன்மைகளைக் கொண்டிருப்பதால், உலகில் நிலைபெற்றுள்ள உயிர்கள் எல்லாம் உன்னை அஞ்சிப் போற்றுகின்றன.","explanation":"The poet Kuṟuṅkōḻiyūr Kiḻār sings in praise of the Cēra king Yāṉaikkaṭcēy Māntarañ Cēral Irumpoṟai. He compares the king's vast qualities—wisdom, mercy, and compassion—to the immeasurable elements of nature, such as the ocean, earth, wind, and sky. The poem describes a land of absolute peace and prosperity where the subjects do not know the heat of oppression, but only the warmth of the sun and cooking fires. They do not know weapons of war, seeing only plows for farming and rainbows in the sky. The king's defense is so absolute that the only ones who 'eat the soil' of his land are pregnant women experiencing cravings, never invading enemies. This poem belongs to the vākai tiṇai (victory and greatness), specifically araca vākai, celebrating the righteous rule (ceṅkōl) and secure protection (ēmam) of a great king.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}